                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f606632-b2d2-4e5a-a39b-9821d11f9c33",
                        "source_entry_id": "7bae724c-a9f3-35e4-b185-1793c72c36be",
                        "target_lang_word": "spongy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spongy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7275e113-3b6d-32a2-9fe0-9d3ca4a06025",
                                        "entry_id": "198752fd-4655-3697-ad46-f6fd9eba4827",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the characteristics of a sponge, namely being absorbent, squishy or porous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34608bb4-e1fc-4b4f-88b6-4238cc4b519a",
                                                "sense_id": "7275e113-3b6d-32a2-9fe0-9d3ca4a06025",
                                                "text": "spongy earth; spongy cake; spongy bones"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98f5ff96-6332-4034-b121-f8062e1b76bf",
                                                "sense_id": "7275e113-3b6d-32a2-9fe0-9d3ca4a06025",
                                                "text": "Though no man lesser fears the Greeks than I\nAs far as toucheth my particular,\nYet, dread Priam,\nThere is no lady of more softer bowels,\nMore spongy to suck in the sense of fear,\nMore ready to cry out 'Who knows what follows?'\nThan Hector is:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5f44891-0a1c-4e94-b621-13e858287af1",
                                                "sense_id": "7275e113-3b6d-32a2-9fe0-9d3ca4a06025",
                                                "text": "[…] there were times when she would lie looking at her, with such a still, watchful, almost dangerous expression, that Helen would sigh, and change her place, as persons do whose breath some cunning orator had been sucking out of them with his spongy eloquence, so that, when he stops, they must get some air and stir about, or they feel as if they should be half-smothered and palsied."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e31fc182-2c50-4769-aa03-ce900a5f63b7",
                                                "sense_id": "7275e113-3b6d-32a2-9fe0-9d3ca4a06025",
                                                "text": "It was easy to realise, too, the need for the overall 40 m.p.h. speed limit; apart from the spongy nature of much of the track bed, the [West Highland] line suffered considerably in the Arctic conditions of last winter, from which it has not yet fully recovered."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c06da4de-65c1-3cca-803b-704370cc5cb2",
                                        "entry_id": "198752fd-4655-3697-ad46-f6fd9eba4827",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wet; drenched; soaked and soft, like sponge; rainy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0a95d0c-6312-412f-bf6a-a7e09d2d7809",
                                                "sense_id": "c06da4de-65c1-3cca-803b-704370cc5cb2",
                                                "text": "Thy banks with pioned and twilled brims,\nWhich spongy April at thy hest betrims,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfcd65cb-5cee-4b56-b940-72b3c63e0c52",
                                                "sense_id": "c06da4de-65c1-3cca-803b-704370cc5cb2",
                                                "text": "Her who still weepes with spungie eyes,\nAnd her who is dry corke, and never cries;\nI can love her, and her, and you and you,\nI can love any, so she be not true."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38604d50-e7a8-4882-b661-66ef818178d1",
                                                "sense_id": "c06da4de-65c1-3cca-803b-704370cc5cb2",
                                                "text": "[…] I was quite tired, and very glad, when we saw Yarmouth. It looked rather spongy and soppy, I thought, as I carried my eye over the great dull waste that lay across the river […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d440564-345f-4d22-a591-fda0d87b30cb",
                                                "sense_id": "c06da4de-65c1-3cca-803b-704370cc5cb2",
                                                "text": "It rains […] most of the fall and winter and much of the spring. It’s a spongy sky you’ll be wearing on your head."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abd31aac-bdba-34d4-ad75-5268af6473d7",
                                        "entry_id": "198752fd-4655-3697-ad46-f6fd9eba4827",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Drunk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4fae036f-e4b4-4fae-8968-7298cdbd41b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "7bae724c-a9f3-35e4-b185-1793c72c36be",
                        "target_lang_word": "squishy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "squishy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "747a9231-bc1f-3100-b20e-44fc9a396c9b",
                                        "entry_id": "5a529d85-b956-32b3-a511-a0658f33b697",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Yielding easily to pressure; very soft."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7c82d17-2c4c-4320-be83-de081ff8a227",
                                                "sense_id": "747a9231-bc1f-3100-b20e-44fc9a396c9b",
                                                "text": "The toy was soft and squishy, making it fun to squeeze."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54a86504-2f36-4fa4-aea7-b801d391ae4d",
                                                "sense_id": "747a9231-bc1f-3100-b20e-44fc9a396c9b",
                                                "text": "The mud was squishy underfoot after the rainstorm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24a16bb0-bd76-4790-a5dd-595f9418160d",
                                                "sense_id": "747a9231-bc1f-3100-b20e-44fc9a396c9b",
                                                "text": "I love how squishy the pillow is—it’s so comfortable to sleep on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f27ec89-f1f4-4a13-9b96-d6f80ef87b1c",
                                                "sense_id": "747a9231-bc1f-3100-b20e-44fc9a396c9b",
                                                "text": "Bread is either cheap (soft, squishy supermarket loaves) or expensive (artisan bakery loaves)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4361e52b-c718-3863-b911-30d19028f534",
                                        "entry_id": "5a529d85-b956-32b3-a511-a0658f33b697",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Yielding easily to pressure; very soft.",
                                            "Soft and wet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially",
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce4204c1-11f2-40fa-9dfa-441a92434ec0",
                                                "sense_id": "4361e52b-c718-3863-b911-30d19028f534",
                                                "text": "Finished with head and hair, the women pulled her up the bank to wash her body, the soft squishy mud registering for the first time on the outer consciousness of Isabelle’s mind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32e859a3-788e-39f1-94e5-c81750f858a3",
                                        "entry_id": "5a529d85-b956-32b3-a511-a0658f33b697",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Subjective or vague."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c69b1967-a338-4445-a018-c6a48688a4f6",
                                                "sense_id": "32e859a3-788e-39f1-94e5-c81750f858a3",
                                                "text": "How does the media love Twitter? Let us count the ways: as a tech platform practically indispensable to the work of newsgathering; as a metrics system designating clear numerical value to once-squishy concepts of popularity and esteem; as a gossip-fueled lunchroom of the elites more or less available for public participation; as an arena for duking out industry controversies ranging from #MeToo to opinions about opinion pages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b59bb8a-20e5-39a7-b876-96917f2aed17",
                                        "entry_id": "5a529d85-b956-32b3-a511-a0658f33b697",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Politically moderate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3c61b15-d313-3de9-9baa-1ed17b9da689",
                                        "entry_id": "5a529d85-b956-32b3-a511-a0658f33b697",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vulnerable to physical damage; having low hit points or defense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9d3ed44-10db-45a3-8564-94a2adb37d27",
                                                "sense_id": "c3c61b15-d313-3de9-9baa-1ed17b9da689",
                                                "text": "Yeah, I’m, like, freaking tissue paper here. Come get the mage, everyone. Pick on the poor squishy mage!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8698dcb-f2bf-472c-879d-aa0380a4a58f",
                                                "sense_id": "c3c61b15-d313-3de9-9baa-1ed17b9da689",
                                                "text": "Telling your healers how well they kept people alive when a battle was difficult is important; or, what a great job your thief did in disarming the traps to get to the raid; clapping your warriors on their backs for maintaining aggro (i.e., keeping the monster targeting them rather than “squishy” mages) or applauding the sorcerers who unloaded incredible amounts of damage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19e1dd9d-a143-4453-a365-5972538b73fa",
                                                "sense_id": "c3c61b15-d313-3de9-9baa-1ed17b9da689",
                                                "text": "What this tells us is that, against PCs equipped to confront a drow shadowblade, a single round's Multiattack is unlikely to deliver a one-hit kill – not unless the target is a squishy wizard or sorcerer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "812cdd80-10f3-3303-a03e-138935384402",
                                        "entry_id": "5a529d85-b956-32b3-a511-a0658f33b697",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Making a squish sound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66f83ff9-56c6-460b-9624-a5c34d0c4977",
                                                "sense_id": "812cdd80-10f3-3303-a03e-138935384402",
                                                "text": "Those darling, squishy little footsteps...Is that you, Punio?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "squishy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bddd98a0-4934-35e3-8abc-9f865fa3bea5",
                                        "entry_id": "5fd47f5a-8ea3-3580-9465-1c86bd8316ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A squeezable stress reliever, especially one made of foam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c684bec9-4587-3d35-b338-590aca458d8d",
                                        "entry_id": "5fd47f5a-8ea3-3580-9465-1c86bd8316ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A term of endearment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28f2bc34-f6b6-49cd-9e17-c113ad51d597",
                                                "sense_id": "c684bec9-4587-3d35-b338-590aca458d8d",
                                                "text": "“It’s going to be fine,” Mother said in her soothing motherly voice. “Is it?” I whispered. “Yes squishy Josh, it will,” she motherlily soothed me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
